# Auto detect text files, normalize to LF in the repo, and check them out as LF
# on EVERY platform. `text=auto` alone only fixes the stored bytes; the working
# tree follows core.eol, which is `native` — so a Windows checkout got CRLF and
# the compiler's golden fixtures stopped matching the LF codegen emits. The
# .pzl and vitest fixtures are compared byte-for-byte the same way.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Highlight .pzl as HTML on github.com (blobs + PR diffs) — repo-wide, the
# pieces registry and demos are .pzl too. Real first-class highlighting needs
# a Linguist PR once .pzl adoption crosses their threshold.
*.pzl linguist-language=HTML
